ttychatter.mailbot 0.4.0
=========================

Command syntax
--------------
- Replaced the public email control syntax with bare control subjects:
  tc:CONFIG, tc:MODELS, tc:CMD, and tc:command args.
- Braced subjects are now reserved for ordinary ttychatter chat sessions:
  tc:{session-name} and tc:{new}.
- tc:{new} now passes no session argument to ttychatter.python, allowing
  ttychatter.python to create its regular default session-YYYY-MM-DD-HH-MM-SS
  name instead of the mailbot inventing the name first.
- Added tc:MODELS as the preferred shorthand for update-models. It runs
  ttychatter.python --update-models and returns models-cache.json when the
  cache can be attached.
- Added tc:CMD as a body-command envelope; the first nonempty body line is used
  as the mailbot command.
- Added direct bare command subjects such as tc:sessions, tc:manpage,
  tc:search TEXT, tc:model-list --all, and tc:routers --model-type chat.
- Added model-list and list-models aliases for ttychatter.python --models so a
  plain tc:MODELS can remain the cache refresh command.

Compatibility
-------------
- Legacy tc:{CONFIG}, tc:{MAILBOT}, and tc:{MAILBOT:command args} subjects are
  still accepted after ALLOWED_FROM passes, but they are no longer the
  documented primary syntax.
- MAILBOT_SUBJECT_TOKEN remains accepted for that legacy command envelope.
- Added MODELS_SUBJECT_TOKEN, default MODELS, and COMMAND_SUBJECT_TOKEN,
  default CMD.

Notes
-----
- The command parser remains allowlisted and non-shell-expanded.
- The mailbot still delegates chat behavior, model-cache updates, model lists,
  memory, sessions, attachments, and OpenRouter interaction to ttychatter.python.

ttychatter.mailbot 0.3.4
=========================

Command syntax
--------------
- Flattened the preferred email control syntax. Use tc:CONFIG for config export/update, tc:MODELS for model-cache refresh with models-cache.json attachment, and tc:<command> for other allowlisted mailbot commands.
- Ordinary ttychatter chat sessions remain braced as tc:{session_name}; tc:{new} still creates an unnamed timestamped session through the usual ttychatter session naming path.
- Added model-list, models-list, list-models, and show-models command aliases for ttychatter.python --models so the reserved tc:MODELS subject can mean cache refresh without ambiguity.
- Commands that need arguments can still take them from the first nonempty message body line, for example Subject: tc:search with the search text in the body.

Compatibility
-------------
- Legacy tc:{CONFIG}, tc:{MAILBOT:command args}, and tc:{MAILBOT} messages remain accepted as compatibility aliases.
- MAILBOT_SUBJECT_TOKEN remains in the config for legacy compatibility, but new mail should not need the MAILBOT namespace.

ttychatter.mailbot 0.3.3
=========================

Diagnostics and config parsing
------------------------------
- --config now makes wrong-user, wrong-HOME, wrong-XDG_CONFIG_HOME, and wrong-config-file mistakes explicit.
- --raw-config prints the actual loaded config file with plaintext IMAP_PASSWORD and SMTP_PASSWORD lines redacted.
- The default config path now resolves TTYCHATTER_MAILBOT_CONFIG first, then XDG_CONFIG_HOME/ttychatter/mailbot/config, then ~/.config/ttychatter/mailbot/config.
- Config parsing now accepts shell-style export KEY=VALUE lines and treats keys case-insensitively, while still writing canonical KEY=VALUE lines.
- Password .gpg default paths now follow the selected config file directory when --config-file, TTYCHATTER_MAILBOT_CONFIG, or XDG_CONFIG_HOME is used.

Notes
-----
- This release is aimed at diagnosing cases where --config appears incomplete while a different file under .config/ttychatter/mailbot contains the expected values.
- If direct gpg --decrypt of the configured password file fails, the mailbot cannot reach IMAP; fix gpg-agent/pinentry first or use a protected plaintext/environment password source.

ttychatter.mailbot 0.3.2
=========================

Diagnostics
-----------
- Added --raw-config to print the actual loaded config file with plaintext IMAP_PASSWORD and SMTP_PASSWORD lines redacted.
- --config now prints PROCESS_USER, HOME, TTYCHATTER_MAILBOT_CONFIG, CONFIG_FILE, CONFIG_EXISTS, CONFIG_READABLE, and CONFIG_MODE before the parsed/effective config.
- Added TTYCHATTER_MAILBOT_CONFIG as an environment override for the default config path. --config-file PATH still has final precedence.

Notes
-----
- --config is intentionally a parsed/effective config report, not a literal file dump. If it looks incomplete while the file on disk looks complete, compare CONFIG_FILE with the file you edited, check command -v ttychatter.mailbot, and compare ttychatter.mailbot --version with ./ttychatter.mailbot --version.

ttychatter.mailbot 0.3.1
=========================

Bug fixes
---------
- Improved GPG password-file failure reporting so --once shows which .gpg file
  failed and prints practical gpg-agent/pinentry recovery commands instead of
  only relaying raw gpg stderr.
- The mailbot now passes GPG_TTY to gpg automatically when the current process
  has a controlling terminal, making manual --once and --set-*-password --gpg
  runs less dependent on shell profile setup.
- --doctor now reports the process user, HOME, and configured password source.
- Rejects empty IMAP_USER/password values and CR/LF in IMAP login values before
  sending LOGIN, replacing confusing server-side BAD errors with local errors.
- Trims trailing CR/LF from decrypted password files while preserving the rest
  of the password.

Notes
-----
- A daemon or cron run without a controlling terminal still needs gpg-agent to
  have the passphrase cached already, or it needs a deployment-specific secret
  source such as a protected plaintext password line or environment override.
- The GPG issue occurs before IMAP login and before any message processing. It
  is not caused by tc:{MAILBOT:...} command dispatch.
- Do not diagnose the normal-user GPG error by switching to root unless the
  service is intended to run as root; root changes HOME, GNUPGHOME, and the
  gpg-agent socket, and may load a different config.

ttychatter.mailbot 0.3.0
=========================

New features
------------
- Added tc:{MAILBOT:...} email control commands, separate from ordinary
  tc:{session} chat messages and tc:{CONFIG} config messages.
- Added tc:{MAILBOT:update-models}, update-model-list, update-model-cache, and
  model-cache aliases. The command runs ttychatter.python --update-models and
  returns models-cache.json by email when the resulting cache exists and is not
  larger than MAX_OUTGOING_ATTACHMENT_BYTES.
- Added tc:{MAILBOT:sessions}, list, list-sessions, and session-list aliases.
  Session listing now includes newest-first session names plus modified time,
  byte count, line count, and short head/tail previews from each session log.
- Added tc:{MAILBOT:manpage}, manual, get-manpage, and fetch-manpage aliases.
  The reply attaches ttychatter.mailbot.1 so the operator can retrieve the
  mailbot manpage by email.
- Added external manpage lookup for the manpage command and --manpage. Lookup
  supports TTYCHATTER_MAILBOT_MANPAGE_FILE, MAILBOT_MANPAGE_FILE, the mailbot
  config directory, the executable directory, XDG/user man1 directories, system
  man1 directories, the current working directory, and matching .1.gz files.
  If no external manpage is found, the embedded fallback is used.
- Added session search and rename commands: search, search-session, and
  rename-session.
- Added allowlisted ttychatter utility commands over email: models, routers,
  favorites, favorite-model, unfavorite-model, test-model, ttyconfig,
  ttydoctor, credits, show-memory, clear-memory, tty-set, and tty-unset.
- Added safe body-line argument completion for commands that commonly need
  arguments, so tc:{MAILBOT:search} can take its search text from the first
  nonempty body line.
- Added local CLI helpers --sessions, --list-sessions, --manpage, and
  --update-models.

Configuration
-------------
- Added MAILBOT_SUBJECT_TOKEN, default MAILBOT.
- Added MAILBOT_MANPAGE_FILE for an explicit external manpage path.
- Added MODEL_CACHE_FILE for the expected ttychatter model cache path when
  ttychatter output does not report one.
- Added TTYCHATTER_CONTROL_TIMEOUT for noninteractive ttychatter utility
  commands.
- Added SESSION_LIST_HEAD_LINES, SESSION_LIST_TAIL_LINES,
  SESSION_LIST_MAX_SESSIONS, and SESSION_PREVIEW_LINE_CHARS for session list
  previews.
- Added SESSION_SEARCH_MAX_MATCHES for bounded session searches.
- Added MAX_COMMAND_OUTPUT_BYTES and MAX_OUTGOING_ATTACHMENT_BYTES for email
  reply and attachment limits.

Compatibility
-------------
- The install name remains ttychatter.mailbot. The temporary
  ttychatter.mailbot.enhanced.py filename was only a staging artifact and is
  not required.
- Existing 0.2.x command-line options remain accepted.
- Existing 0.2.x config keys remain accepted.
- REPLY_METHOD remains accepted as an alias for SEND_METHOD.
- SENDMAIL_PATH remains accepted as an alias for SENDMAIL.
- Ordinary tc:{session} mail continues to delegate chat behavior to
  ttychatter.python --loopback.

Safety notes
------------
- tc:{MAILBOT:...} commands are honored only after the normal ALLOWED_FROM
  sender check passes.
- Control commands are allowlisted and are not shell-expanded.
- TTYCHATTER_EXTRA_ARGS is used only for ordinary loopback chat calls, not for
  mailbot utility/control calls.
- tty-set refuses OPENROUTER_API_KEY and API_KEY by email; set secrets locally.
- --dry-run does not send replies, mark messages seen, record processed
  Message-IDs, replace config, rename sessions, or refresh model caches.
- update-models returns command output even when the cache cannot be attached,
  and reports the cache path or attachment error in the reply body.

Notes
-----
- Install the manpage as ttychatter.mailbot.1. If a generated artifact is named
  ttychatter.mailbot.1.updated, copy or install it under the canonical name, or
  point MAILBOT_MANPAGE_FILE directly at that file.
- The mailbot remains an IMAP poller and ttychatter transport adapter. It still
  does not implement OpenRouter request logic directly.

ttychatter.mailbot 0.2.1
=========================

Bug fixes
---------
- Rewrote sender allowlist handling so an exact ALLOWED_FROM address is honored.
- Removed the overbroad self-sender rejection that blocked setups using the same local mailbox for MAIL_FROM and ALLOWED_FROM.
- ALLOWED_FROM now accepts comma, semicolon, or whitespace separated addresses, plus the wildcard * for temporary testing.
- --list-candidates now prints the configured allowlist in sender skip reasons, making allowlist bugs visible without marking messages read.

Notes
-----
- For production, a distinct MAIL_FROM such as ttychatter@example.org is still cleaner. The allowlist, processed Message-ID database, and strict tc:{...} subject parser remain the real mailbot safety controls.

ttychatter.mailbot 0.2.0
=========================

Bug fixes
---------
- Rewrote IMAP candidate inspection to use BODY.PEEK[] instead of RFC822/BODY[] fetches.
- Dry-run no longer marks unread messages as read merely by inspecting them.
- Skipped messages are left unread so the operator can see and correct sender/subject/config problems.
- IMAP and GPG runtime errors are caught and printed as clear command-line errors instead of Python tracebacks.

New features
------------
- Added --list-candidates to show unread candidate messages, From, Subject, Message-ID, and skip/match reason without modifying mailbox state.
- Added tc:{CONFIG} mail workflow.
- tc:{CONFIG} with no config attachment replies with the current mailbot config as a text attachment.
- tc:{CONFIG} with an edited config attachment applies the new config, after creating a timestamped backup.
- Dry-run for tc:{CONFIG} never writes config or marks the message read.
- Plaintext IMAP_PASSWORD and SMTP_PASSWORD lines are redacted from config exports.
- Added CONFIG_SUBJECT_TOKEN config key, default CONFIG.
- Added CONFIG_UPDATE_REQUIRES_ATTACHMENT config key for documentation and future policy tightening.

Notes
-----
- tc:{CONFIG} is only honored after the normal ALLOWED_FROM check passes.
- Config editing by email is intentionally attachment-based so a normal message body cannot accidentally replace the config.
- The mailbot remains an IMAP poller and ttychatter transport adapter. It still does not implement OpenRouter logic directly.
